  "task": {
    "objective": "Supply two cloth orders per villager before the fair closes. Growing flax, borrowing tools, exchanging material, repairing shared machines and committing labor all compete with private delivery deadlines.",
    "natural_termination": "Natural completion when every villager has delivered two orders, or at step 80 when the fair closes. H=96 is a separate upper bound; natural cause has priority and is absorbing.",
    "interaction": "Actual adjacent tools can be lent, returned and recalled. Spinner and loom have exclusive job/output slots and depleting condition. Two-step labor promises may advance another owners job and block the helpers next action. Finite material gifts and repairs enable partners production.",
    "observation_access": "Map, positions, materials, plots, machine condition, job reservation, output, labor and tool loans are public. A role alone knows its private early-delivery deadline. Tool owners are fixed common knowledge 0 for sickle and 1 for shuttle."
  },
